    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d128">

                <pb facs="0227" n="121" sameAs="frus:frus1933-39/pg121"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">800.51W89 U.S.S.R./85a: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Ambassador in the Soviet
                        Union</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Bullitt</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1934-07-21T16:00:00-04:00">July 21, 1934—4
                            p.m.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>170. Troyanovsky called at the Department today and arrangements were made for a
                    meeting at the Department on Wednesday for a general discussion of the question
                    of settlement of debts and claims.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Hull</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
